From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dmime: performance (IsPlaying, ports, PChannels, time and rhythm, PlaySegmentEx / StopEx, Invalidate, SetParam, GetParamEx, ...), segment and segment state members

Performance:
- IsPlaying looks at the segment states that still have a tick or end
  message pending. SetParam goes to the control segment, then the primary
  segment, as GetParam does; GetParamEx finds the track by its virtual
  track id in the playing segment states (without id it is GetParam).
- AddPort remembers the ports, RemovePort only accepts them and drops the
  channels assigned to the port. The last two PChannel blocks cannot be
  assigned as a block, the last one can be assigned channel by channel but
  not read back (the todo_wine conformance tests).
- GetQueueTime (latency plus bumper), AdjustTime (offsets the performance
  time), GetResolvedTime (after prepare / queue / latency time, next grid,
  beat or measure), TimeToRhythm / RhythmToTime (time signature of the
  performance or the one given, 4/4 with two grids by default),
  MIDIToMusic / MusicToMIDI for the fixed play mode. Other play modes need
  scale tables and stay E_NOTIMPL with a FIXME.
- PlaySegmentEx honours the start time, DMUS_SEGF_REFTIME, the grid / beat /
  measure (of the playing primary segment) / after-prepare / after-queue /
  after-latency resolutions and DMUS_SEGF_DEFAULT, and the audio path.
  StopEx stops a segment state, a segment, everything on an audio path or
  everything. Invalidate drops the queued track messages from the given time
  and plays the tracks again from there. GetSegmentState checks the time.
- The performance tool's Flush is S_OK; as the last tool of a message it
  accepts the tempo, time signature, lyric and dirty messages the tracks
  send now (nothing to do) and plays sysex messages to the port.
- FIXMEs on already working code (Stop, notification types, CloseDown,
  audio path creation, default audio path, SetGraph) are dropped.

Segment and segment state:
- InitPlay returns the placeholder state the tests describe (no FIXME);
  a new segment is one tick long; SetParam follows GetParam's index rules
  (E_POINTER without type, DMUS_E_TRACK_NOT_FOUND); SetPChannelsUsed,
  SetTrackConfig (class, group, index, flags on/off), notification types
  (forwarded to the tracks), GetAudioPathConfig (loaded from an embedded
  DMAP form, DMUS_E_NO_AUDIOPATH_CONFIG otherwise). Compose stays
  E_NOTIMPL with a FIXME; the graph is released with the segment.
- The segment state keeps the track configuration (SetTrackConfig; tracks
  without PLAY_ENABLED are not played), the audio path it plays on and
  reports the seek position; GetObjectInPath asks that audio path (or the
  default one). Tracks are played with the time offset of the segment start
  minus its start point, as the tests expect.

The todo_wine marks which pass now are removed.
